  * A. fewer jobs and a surplus of labour
    B. more jobs and a shortage of labour
    C. more jobs and a surplus of labour
    D. fewer jobs and a shortage of labour

=== step 26 · block 4 "Market Failure in the Labour Market" · quiz index 26
DIAGRAM title: Immobility: Two Regions
description: IAL 3.3.4 · 4a: demand for machinists falls in one region and rises in another. If workers cannot move, the wage gap does not close, and if pay stays at the old wage in both there are jobless workers in one region and vacancies in the other.
checklist: ["Two regional labour markets with the same supply and the same starting point","North: D shifts left; the wage falls to $10, or at $12 12,000 are jobless","South: D shifts right; the wage rises to $14, or at $12 12,000 posts are empty","The gap persists because workers cannot move between the two"]
view: {"label":"North: demand falls"}
  svg text: The North: workshops close | Wage ($ an hour) | Machinists (thousands) | D | S | D₁ | 12 | 36 | 10 | 28 | 24 | Wage $10 if it falls; at $12, 12,000 jobless. | The workers cannot move South.
view: {"label":"South: demand rises"}
  svg text: The South: orders grow | Wage ($ an hour) | Machinists (thousands) | D | S | D₁ | 12 | 36 | 14 | 44 | 48 | Wage $14 if it rises; at $12, 12,000 vacancies. | Idle workers in the North could fill them.
